From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:45:16 +0800
Subject: cli/service: restart the background server when idle

`ocelot service set restart idle` (default `immediate`, upstream's behavior) makes the automatic
restarts wait until no session has run for 30 s:

- A new binary installed at the server's own path (install script, `ocelot upgrade`,
  autoupdate) restarts the server once idle; with `immediate` nothing happens, as upstream.
- A client of another version (TUI) no longer replaces a busy server: it connects to it and the
  server restarts into the new version once idle. Idle servers are replaced right away.

`ocelot service restart --when-idle` asks for the same regardless of the setting; plain
`ocelot service restart` still restarts at once. A detached waiter (`--idle-waiter`) polls
/api/session/active and replaces the server like a newer client does (terminals handed over);
its progress is `<registration>.restart`, shown by `ocelot service status`.

Ocelot-Patch: cli/restart-when-idle

